        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Parachute Repair Manual Page 7-28</title>\n  <script src=\"https://polyfill.io/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6\"></script>\n  <script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      background: #fff;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    }\n    .page {\n      width: 1350px;\n      min-height: 1800px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      padding: 98px 82px 52px;\n    }\n    .columns {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 660px 1fr;\n      gap: 32px;\n      align-items: start;\n    }\n    .placeholder {\n      position: relative;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      border: 1.5px solid #111;\n      border-radius: 11px;\n      background:\n        linear-gradient(110deg, rgba(54,130,138,.72) 0 8%, rgba(143,148,142,.48) 9% 26%, rgba(202,201,193,.50) 27% 74%, rgba(31,126,143,.70) 75% 100%),\n        linear-gradient(145deg, #4f9a9e, #d6d2c6 45%, #5e9aa0);\n      color: rgba(0,0,0,.72);\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 15px;\n    }\n    .placeholder .tag {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 20px;\n      top: 19px;\n      width: 43px;\n      height: 43px;\n      border-radius: 50%;\n      background: #b84235;\n      border: 2px solid #7c2b25;\n      color: white;\n      text-align: center;\n      line-height: 39px;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      font-size: 22px;\n      text-shadow: 1px 1px #555;\n    }\n    .placeholder .caption {\n      position: absolute;\n      width: 100%;\n      bottom: 13px;\n      text-align: center;\n      color: rgba(0,0,0,.42);\n      font-style: italic;\n      font-size: 14px;\n    }\n    .photo-m { height: 500px; }\n    .photo-p { height: 454px; }\n    .photo-n { height: 497px; margin-top: 30px; }\n    .photo-o { height: 497px; margin-top: 28px; }\n    .step {\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 1.36;\n      margin: 15px 0 0 27px;\n      text-indent: -26px;\n    }\n    .step.long {\n      margin-top: 32px;\n      max-width: 645px;\n    }\n    h2 {\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      line-height: 1.08;\n      margin: 37px 0 17px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n    h3 {\n      font-size: 28px;\n      font-style: italic;\n      margin: 17px 0 14px;\n    }\n    .inspection {\n      margin-top: 18px;\n    }\n    .inspection h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 14px;\n    }\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 0 39px;\n      padding: 0;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 1.28;\n    }\n    li {\n      padding-left: 10px;\n      margin-bottom: 12px;\n    }\n    .details {\n      margin-top: 0;\n      font-size: 24px;\n      line-height: 1.27;\n    }\n    .details li { margin-bottom: 13px; }\n    .section-title {\n      margin-top: 39px;\n      margin-bottom: 14px;\n    }\n    .procedure {\n      margin-top: 40px;\n    }\n    .procedure p {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 1.3;\n      text-align: justify;\n    }\n    .disassembly {\n      margin-top: 40px;\n    }\n    .disassembly ol {\n      margin: 0 0 0 35px;\n      padding-left: 25px;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      line-height: 1.31;\n    }\n    .disassembly li {\n      padding-left: 12px;\n      margin: 0;\n    }\n    .page-no {\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 25px;\n      margin-top: 53px;\n    }\n    em { font-style: italic; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <div class=\"columns\">\n      <section class=\"left\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder photo-m\">\n          <span class=\"tag\">M</span>\n          <span class=\"caption\">[Photo: marked parachute fabric panel]</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"step\">11.&nbsp; Trim the top and bottom edges as marked. <em>[Figure N]</em></p>\n\n        <div class=\"placeholder photo-n\">\n          <span class=\"tag\">N</span>\n          <span class=\"caption\">[Photo: ruler marking canopy seam]</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"step long\">12.&nbsp; Pin the top seam back onto the top panel. Sew in place<br>\n          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;with either the single needle or if available, with the<br>\n          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;double needle machine and puller. <em>[Figure O]</em> Repeat<br>\n          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;with the bottom seam.</p>\n\n        <div class=\"placeholder photo-o\">\n          <span class=\"tag\">O</span>\n          <span class=\"caption\">[Photo: sewing machine stitching canopy fabric]</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"step\">13.&nbsp; Inspect finished work. <em>[Figure P]</em></p>\n        <div class=\"page-no\">7-28</div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"right\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder photo-p\">\n          <span class=\"tag\">P</span>\n          <span class=\"caption\">[Photo: finished repaired canopy panel]</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"inspection\">\n          <h3>Inspection</h3>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Seam alignment should be straight.</li>\n            <li>Check the tension of the replaced rib material.</li>\n            <li>Make sure the seams are restitched correctly.</li>\n            <li>Verify that the crossport is cut correctly.</li>\n            <li>The line attachment tape must be replaced correctly<br>with no twists in the suspension line.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <h2 class=\"section-title\">Square Canopy—Pilot Chute Attachment Point<br>Repair</h2>\n\n        <ul class=\"details\">\n          <li>Applicable Products: Square main canopies</li>\n          <li>Description: Repair of the main canopy pilot chute<br>attachment point.</li>\n          <li>Authorized Repairmen: FAA Master Parachute Rigger</li>\n          <li>Materials: E thread; fabric—type and color to match,<br>reinforcing tape—type and color to match, reinforcing<br>fabric—type and color to match</li>\n          <li>Machines: 301 straight stitch—medium duty 7–11<br>SPI, 308 zigzag—medium duty 7–11 SPI, 1 inch ×<br>42 stitch bar tack</li>\n          <li>Equipment: Scissors, seam ripper, marking pencil,<br>and 12–inch ruler</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"procedure\">\n          <h3>Procedure</h3>\n          <p>This repair is quite common. If the canopy is inspected regularly, the beginnings of the damage will be noticed and a simple re-stitching will solve the problem. However, many times it is not and the resultant damage is quite extensive requiring repair of the rib, as well as the top panel.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"disassembly\">\n          <h3>Disassembly</h3>\n          <ol>\n            <li>Inspect the area to determine the extent of the damage.<br><em>[Figure A]</em> If the stitching that holds the attachment<br>point to the canopy is simply coming loose, re-stitch<br>as per the original.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
